====================================================================================================
hembed / THM-527 Part A: does a good period embed into a lonely real time?  1/14 = 0.07143
  setup: e = co-offset cluster (incl 0), Vmax >= max e, speeds v_i = Vmax - e_i
====================================================================================================

  Vmax=1000 >> spread 30 (clean):  Vmax=1000, spread(e)=30, #good-periods=943
    TRUE M(S) = max_tau min nearInt(v_i tau) = 0.49227  (>=1/14 LRC-OK) at tau=0.00051
    widest good period j=1, gap=0.9700 (slack over 1/7 = 0.8271), phi*=0.5150
    NAIVE embed tau=(j+phi)/Vmax=0.00152: min nearInt(v_i tau) = 0.46955 (clears 1/14)
    coupling error e_max*phi/Vmax = 0.0155  vs gap slack/2 = 0.4136  (slack absorbs error)
    BEST tau in ruler cell [j/Vmax, (j+1)/Vmax): min nearInt = 0.47715 at tau=0.001523 (>=1/14)

